  {
    "sha": "f54a11059a2d78648ecdb188c6b14d834402cf0f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGY1NGExMTA1OWEyZDc4NjQ4ZWNkYjE4OGM2YjE0ZDgzNDQwMmNmMGY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T17:23:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T17:23:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pathkernel): one completeness guard on the whole centre area\n\nReview of PR #4189, finding 1: the ring planner narrowed the guard's\narea by the first offset, so a first offset above the tool radius left\nthe strip at the wall uncut with a done verdict (disc, tool radius 3,\nfirst offset 5, step 2: 201 mm2).\n\nThe rule for the class: cover::judge is the one guard of both planners.\nIt reads the region's own centre area and the curves of the finished\nset; no planner passes it an area. A clearing ring choice whose first\noffset is above the tool radius is refused (WALL_STRIP_UNCUT). A ring\ncount names the uncut area in a note.\n\nPins: the review case, and property grids for rings (both references,\ndisc and island pocket) and rows: done implies at most 0.1 mm2 uncut,\nmeasured on its own.\n\nRefs #4176\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
