  {
    "sha": "74766eaa57edc0cd6ab220b7dcf46164b764cfcc",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDc0NzY2ZWFhNTdlZGMwY2Q2YWIyMjBiN2RjZjQ2MTY0Yjc2NGNmY2M",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T17:23:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T17:23:54Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pathkernel): name each dropped mark; pin closing rings and open-ring marks\n\nReview of PR #4189, findings 2 to 4:\n- 2: nothing that a planner made is dropped without a note. When the\n  curve checks refuse a raw curve, its note also names the marks on it\n  that are not kept (unit pin a_refused_curve_names_its_marks_in_its_note).\n- 3: the closing ring of a rows choice runs round each loop of the area,\n  an island included (pin the_closing_ring_of_rows_runs_round_each_island_too).\n- 4: a full-width stretch on an open ring round a part is named (pin\n  a_full_width_stretch_on_an_open_ring_round_a_part_is_named).\n\nRefs #4176\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "3cbaf0eec4c1170c4767ca53e6341ba14728b5d2",
